    "summary": "High‑energy second set with blistering China Cat > Rider; solid overall show",
    "blurb": "The band delivers a scorching China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue backed by tight rhythm and Brent’s sparkling keys. Althea, Lazy Lightning and Franklin's Tower shine, while Peggy‑O and Far From Me lose momentum. The recommended soundboard is clear but the piano sits a bit forward.",
    "review": "On July 1, 1980 at the San Diego Sports Arena the Dead turned in a lively two‑set marathon that still feels fresh. Set 2 bursts open with an “on‑fire” China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition, where Jerry’s soaring solos and Bob’s vocal interplay lift the groove into a classic high point. Brent Mydland adds his usual sparkle on keys—though at moments his piano sits a touch too forward—but his energy fuels strong renditions of Althea, Lazy Lightning and Franklin's Tower. The first set is solid, though the later selections of Peggy‑O and Far From Me drag the flow down a notch. Overall the performance is tight, energetic, and worth revisiting, especially with the best‑sounding soundboard capture that balances the band well despite minor volume quirks.\n\nFans looking for the clearest listen should gravitate to the Cole‑archived SBD (gd80-07-01.sbd.cole.9361.sbeok.shnf), which preserves the blistering China Cat sequence and captures the concert’s vibe without the vocal‑overpower issues that plague some other mixes.",
